<p class="has-shippori-antique-b-1-font-family has-small-font-size" style="padding-top:var(--wp--preset--spacing--50);padding-right:0;padding-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--50);padding-left:0">  Marcus Vance (b. 1994) is a Toronto-based interdisciplinary performance artist. His practice fuses techniques in movement, experimental video, lens-based media, and large-scale drawing.<br><br>  Thematically, his work explores physical displacement, spatial duration, and how technology mediates the relationship between the human body and urban environments. Vance completed his degree in Media and Digital Cultures before establishing a studio practice focused on video art and performance archives. <br><br>  His work has been exhibited at the Power Plant Contemporary Art Gallery, Trinity Square Video, and the Art Museum at the University of Toronto.<br></p>
